{
  "algorithm": "catboost",
  "name": "CatBoost",
  "description": "Gradient-boosted symmetric trees with native categorical handling.",
  "preprocessing": "`CatBoostPipeline`: selects the feature columns, passes the market identifier to CatBoost as a native categorical feature and leaves missing numeric values to CatBoost's native handling (no imputation). Loss RMSE, seed 42. When the shape constraint is on, monotone_constraints = +1 for the volume features in `features.MONOTONE_INCREASING`. With `log_target`, the estimator is wrapped in `TransformedTargetRegressor(log1p, expm1)`; every metric is reported in guests. With the `floor_zero` policy the pipeline is wrapped in `NonNegative`, which floors predictions at 0 (raw negatives are still counted in the metadata).",
